<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <title>OpenDSA Registration Complete</title>
</head>
<body style="font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, sans-serif; padding: 24px; color: #222;">
  <h2 style="color: #5cb85c; margin-top: 0;">Registration successful</h2>
  <p style="line-height: 1.5;">
    OpenDSA has been registered with <strong><%= @lms_instance.issuer %></strong>.
  </p>
  <table style="border-collapse: collapse; margin: 16px 0;">
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 4px 16px 4px 0; font-weight: 600;">LmsInstance ID</td>
      <td style="padding: 4px 0;"><code><%= @lms_instance.id %></code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 4px 16px 4px 0; font-weight: 600;">Client ID</td>
      <td style="padding: 4px 0;"><code><%= @lms_instance.client_id %></code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td style="padding: 4px 16px 4px 0; font-weight: 600;">Issuer</td>
      <td style="padding: 4px 0;"><code><%= @lms_instance.issuer %></code></td>
    </tr>
  </table>
  <p style="line-height: 1.5;">
    The platform administrator must now review and activate the new tool
    registration in the LMS. After activation, instructors can add OpenDSA
    to their courses via Deep Linking.
  </p>
  <script>
    (function() {
      var target = window.opener || window.parent;
      if (target) {
        target.postMessage({ subject: 'org.imsglobal.lti.close' }, '*');
      }
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
